+
+Static specialization binds HIR shapes, not generic launch-grid dimensions.
+For the legacy module, layout propagation may flatten or normalize TensorIR
+iteration space, so the compile-free seam retains the accepted producer-owned
+positive `x`, `y=1,z=1` rule; the backend-ON facade parity test freezes
+`[8,8]`, tile `16` as grid `{4,1,1}`. The separately versioned dense fused
+pointwise module has a stronger normalized law: preparation requires exactly
+one `dim_000` tile, a positive power of two no larger than the product of the
+static shape, and a resulting grid within signed-int32 and target limits.
+Finalization requires exactly
+`{ceil(product(shape) / dim_000), 1, 1}`. Preparation itself invokes no
+producer, filesystem, subprocess, CUDA API, or GPU. The facade may invoke the
+CPU compiler and assembler subprocess, but it never initializes CUDA or
+executes on a GPU.
+
+### Bounded fused pointwise frontend v2
+
+`FusedPointwiseV2` is private compiler analysis, not a new public compiler
+facade or wire type. It emits entry `pypto_fused_pointwise_v2` and metadata
+schema 2. It accepts one Opaque function with 1 through 16 exact `In` tensor
+parameters, 1 through 64 direct SSA assignments, and one return of the final
+assignment. All values are the same plain, fully static, contiguous BF16 or
+FP32 tensor of rank 1 through 32, with no MemRef, view, broadcast, dynamic
+extent, attribute, keyword argument, or mutation.
+
+The registered HIR allowlist is `tensor.add`, `tensor.adds`, `tensor.sub`,
+`tensor.subs`, `tensor.mul`, `tensor.muls`, `tensor.neg`, `tensor.exp`,
+`tensor.recip`, and `tensor.rsqrt`; operator identity is checked through the
+registry. Every assignment after the first must consume the exact immediately
+preceding result. Other tensor operands may be direct parameters, older or
+forward intermediate references are rejected, and every parameter must be
+used. Scalar forms require one exact, same-dtype `ConstFloat` whose value stays
+finite in its declared tensor dtype. They emit canonical scalar `constant` plus
+`splat` operations; `tensor.recip` emits TensorIR `reciprocal`. All attributes
+and keyword arguments, including `high_precision`, are rejected rather than
+silently discarded.
+
+The exact legacy two-input add form is classified as `LegacyStaticAddV1` before
+V2 analysis. Its `pypto_vector_add` source, schema-1 projection bytes, callable
+ABI and producer behavior remain frozen. This CPU/compiler contract proves
+bounded syntax, deterministic identities, ABI validation and Cubin production;
+it does not prove FP32/BF16 transcendental numerical correctness, CUDA launch,
+or performance. Those require a separate real-SM120 correctness gate.
 
